WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:15.030
- Welcome to another episode
on my channel Firm Learning.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.590
My name is Heinrich and
as you know, on my channel

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:20.220
I want to help you to become successful

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.860
in the first years of your career.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:26.140
Here today I'm once again
back at my university

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:29.160
of Munich, this is the
place where I studied

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.320
business and philosophy
during my undergrad.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.380
And the topic of today's
video is private university

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.520
versus public university.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.450
Private school versus public school.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:43.150
And the question is, which one is better?

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:46.770
Is private university
really worth the money?

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:50.850
Is it worth the investment
of your time, of your effort?

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:54.130
And I want to reflect on this exactly here

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:55.630
at my old university.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:59.040
Because indeed, while I
did my bachelor in Munich,

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.930
in parallel to that I
completed a semester abroad

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:04.140
at Bocconi University in Milan,

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.000
which is a private business school,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.380
and then later continued
to do a master in finance

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:13.540
and accounting at the London
School of Economics in London.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.210
So indeed the question
is, which one is better?

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:18.610
This is what we're going
to talk about today.

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:21.670
So before we jump into the
details of the pros and cons

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:24.090
of public versus private universities,

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:26.160
I first wanna specify a bit more

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.490
what exactly I mean by
this public university.

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:32.510
Because I know that here there
are significant differences,

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:35.150
also country by country, especially also,

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:36.530
on the wider regions.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.720
So for instance I know that for sure if,

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.577
in a US context, you talk
about a public university,

00:01:42.577 --> 00:01:44.570
the universities that there you would have

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.850
in your mind are probably
very different than what

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:49.130
you would talk about in,
for instance, in German,

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:51.120
or broader European context.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.290
Because indeed here in
Germany public universities,

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:55.840
like the University of Munich,

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.010
are quite good indeed.

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:00.380
And indeed this is I trust
similar in many other

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:01.710
European countries as well.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.870
So in the context of this
video I will rather talk

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.410
about this more European type of system

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:09.300
whereby the public university
might not necessarily have

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:12.670
the reputation of some of
the very best private ones,

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:14.730
they're still considered to be good,

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:16.600
and to some extent also competitive,

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:19.150
and some of them even target universities,

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:20.951
but we are going to
talk about this concept

00:02:20.951 --> 00:02:23.320
a bit more in a couple of minutes.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:26.220
I will now talk about
four aspects where private

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.380
universities potentially
are a bit different

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:29.970
than public universities.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:33.260
And the first one is the
richness of experience.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:35.580
And this is now especially
relevant when you compare

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.430
private business schools

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:40.550
to public, big universities
like for instance

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:41.830
the University of Munich.

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:44.540
And for me one of the
key reasons why I decided

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.160
to start my undergraduate
studies here in Munich,

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.940
compared to for instance
also some German private

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:52.390
business schools that
exist for sure as well,

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:55.789
was really the opportunity
to study different types

00:02:55.789 --> 00:02:58.670
of subjects, different
types of degree programs.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:01.690
And personally I did indeed
study business and philosophy,

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:03.620
but even if you're not willing to complete

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:06.770
two full degrees, if you're
just enrolled in a business

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.940
program, and then just
take individual lectures,

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:12.960
individual classes on
some other topics as well,

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:16.850
for me this was one of the
key parts of the experience,

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:19.350
of studying in an undergraduate degree,

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:22.730
and this is of course
often not really possible

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:24.220
in a private business school.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.110
Maybe if you compare
this to the London School

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:28.710
of Economics and Political Sciences,

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:30.620
which is the full name of the school,

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.940
there yes there were
some other opportunities,

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:36.090
but for instance at my MBA,
I only had the opportunity

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:37.750
to take business classes.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.650
And while these were
for sure high quality,

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.290
and very interesting and
relevant business classes,

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:44.758
there I missed this
opportunity to go beyond

00:03:44.758 --> 00:03:46.620
my core subject.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:49.780
Same thing was true at
the University of Bocconi,

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:52.157
which is indeed an Italian
business school as well.

00:03:52.157 --> 00:03:54.890
And this then also
translates just to the size

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:56.880
and magnitude of university.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:01.140
So here in Munich, 50,000
students are studying.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:04.820
This comes with lots of
extracurricular activities,

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:07.610
organizations, other
opportunities that you could

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:10.327
be part of, in parallel
to studying in university.

00:04:10.327 --> 00:04:12.790
And while things like that exist as well

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:17.050
in these private schools,
these are often much smaller,

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:19.350
and by that also just the sheer amount

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:22.060
and opportunities of
organizations, activities,

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:25.470
societies, that you can
be part of, is limited,

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:27.610
this is at least what I strongly felt.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:29.060
Next point I wanna talk about

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.610
is the quality of the teaching.

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.870
The quality of the education
that is being delivered to you.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.450
And here I'd assume that
many people would argue

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:39.800
that yes the private
universities have an advantage,

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.150
and of course this might also be the case,

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.540
especially because due
to the better funding

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:47.240
of the private universities,
there you will often have

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:50.500
smaller group sizes instead
of sitting in a class

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:55.360
with 800, 900 other students
as I often experienced it,

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:57.180
here at the University of Munich,

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.600
in universities like
the LSE where I studied,

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.850
or Boccani in Milan, or the
later of course also the MBA,

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:06.070
the class sizes were
significantly smaller,

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:09.140
contributing to a better
learning environment, I'd say.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.040
And here now, right now,
I'm standing in front

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.700
of the business faculty where
I studied here in Munich,

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.630
and indeed it was the case
that while the classes

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:20.320
were often larger, especially the later,

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:24.600
in the third, fourth, fifth,
sixth semester of university,

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.810
you had courses, you
had seminars where then

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:29.200
the group sizes were smaller as well,

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.150
so I wouldn't say it's
this black and white

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:33.570
when you compare these
two types of universities,

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:36.820
though indeed on average,
I would say it is correct

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:40.780
that these interactions are
richer, are in smaller groups,

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:42.500
in the private universities.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.340
But here also I wanna say that in general

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:47.750
the quality of the lectures,
the quality of the teachings,

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:50.533
this had not a lower quality in Munich,

00:05:50.533 --> 00:05:53.130
here I also had some excellent lectures,

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:56.450
excellent classes delivered
by excellent professors,

00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:59.120
so this I'd say was rather similar,

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:01.560
though again quality of the groups,

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.530
smaller group sizes, this
is really what you get

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:07.460
as a pro in this private context.

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:10.490
The next thing I wanna talk
about are student fees.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:13.340
And indeed student fees are
often one of the first things

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:15.940
that come to your mind when you talk about

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:17.850
these private universities.

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.890
And indeed this is of course true,

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:23.350
so when I studied here
at University of Munich,

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:26.380
I almost paid no student fees at all.

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:29.570
Essentially studying
at a public university

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:31.800
in Germany is for free.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:35.270
So this is of course different
to the private universities.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:37.640
When I completed my master
in accounting and finance

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:41.160
in London, I paid over 20,000 pounds,

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:43.200
British pounds, in student fees.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.460
And I recently checked again, the webpage,

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:49.230
today it costs even over 30,000 pounds.

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:52.800
This is of course a crazy
amount, and can be very

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:56.500
detrimental for other people
trying to study in this way.

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:57.650
So how can you do it?

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:59.440
What can you do to finance this?

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:02.920
And indeed there are lots of
opportunities for scholarships,

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:05.760
I would encourage you really
to check out scholarships

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:07.200
that might be available to you,

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:10.210
I was privileged enough to
pay at least a significant

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:13.830
portion of the total student
fees with scholarship programs,

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:16.350
of course the exact programs
that are available to you

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.830
depend on your country, on the university,

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:21.310
on your region, so do this research.

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:24.500
Though my opinion also is
if you really wanna do it,

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.730
if you have a dream university
where you want to study,

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:29.840
there are ways to make it work.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:33.690
I would very likely not, not
study at such a university,

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:35.140
only due to the student fees,

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:37.160
there are often ways to finance it,

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:39.870
and indeed after you
study at such university,

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:42.770
especially if you study something
in the area of business,

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:45.030
you really often have
opportunities to then also

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:47.760
recoup, remake the money rather quickly

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:51.110
after graduating, at least
if you then also have

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:54.000
the goal to move into
one of these high paced

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.050
careers that then provide
you with the salaries

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:59.340
that would also enable you
to pay back the student loans

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:01.890
that you might potentially
take to finance this.

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:04.640
The other question that of
course people have in mind

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:07.780
when talking about public
versus private university,

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:10.400
is the whole discussion of target schools,

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:13.570
is the whole discussion of
whether or not it really helps

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:16.730
your career to study at
these private schools

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:20.280
potentially because they are
considered a target school,

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:23.310
which is a school that
is a preferred university

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:25.200
for employers to hire from.

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:27.480
And indeed now reflecting
on my experience here,

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:30.180
I think the first insight
is that you will always need

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:32.930
to distinguish local target schools

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:34.780
from global target schools,

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.860
because the University of
Munich, even though it is

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:42.020
a public university, could
be considered a target school

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:46.040
in Germany, so this
university has the reputation

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:48.750
in Germany that it is one of
the leading business schools.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:52.030
And indeed all these employers
that we so frequently talk

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:55.260
about on this channel, like
the MBB consulting firms,

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:59.150
McKinsey, BCG, Bain, and so
on, they do like to hire people

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:02.290
from the University of
Munich, and indeed I was hired

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:05.260
for an internship at
McKinsey when I was studying

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:06.687
in the middle of my bachelor here.

00:09:06.687 --> 00:09:10.540
Though the truth is also probably
if you go beyond Germany,

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:12.290
if you go beyond the country,

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:14.840
very few people will really know

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:16.060
the University of Munich.

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:18.117
So it is a local target school.

00:09:18.117 --> 00:09:20.110
And now you can compare this to a school

00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:22.070
like the London School of Economics,

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:24.090
in the UK, in England,

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:26.770
this is of course
university which is probably

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:30.270
well known also far outside of the UK.

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:33.010
Many people in many
other countries will know

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:35.810
this university, so this
university that might be

00:09:35.810 --> 00:09:38.600
considered an international target school.

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:41.440
And if you want this type of reputation,

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:43.568
if you want to study at university,

00:09:43.568 --> 00:09:46.070
with a reputation that
exceeds the boundaries

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:48.020
of your region, of your country,

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:50.600
it might be worthwhile to go there as well

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:53.120
and yes of course in
terms of target schools,

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:55.170
in terms of later
potentially also applying

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:58.900
to an MBA, or to other
larger global firms,

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:01.500
this might be helpful,
though I would argue

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:05.490
most of your career ambitions
can very much be fulfilled

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:09.290
with studying at a public
university which is a local

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:10.920
target school as well.

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:13.520
So I hope that these
different considerations,

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:15.420
these different dimensions
that I looked at

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:18.160
are helpful to you if
you are in the position

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:20.220
to now ask yourself
whether you'd like to study

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:22.600
at a public or private university.

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:24.180
But what is my personal conclusion?

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:26.660
What is my reflection on this question?

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:28.850
And personally, I would not have wanted

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.200
to miss my time in Munich.

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:34.610
It was for me an extremely
remarkable and formative time.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:37.600
And indeed just also from
the cost perspective,

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:40.070
given that the undergraduate
degree usually goes

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:43.100
three to four years, now
the need of having to pay

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:45.420
students fees for all this time,

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:49.450
this is of course insane, and
it's arguable whether you will

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:52.940
recoup this financial burden
then later in your job.

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:55.730
But what I think could be the sweet spot

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:58.380
is to indeed do the undergraduate degree

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:02.680
at a public university,
benefit from the lower cost,

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:05.930
from this very remarkable
experience that you get there,

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:09.310
and then get for the private
university the master degree,

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:12.080
because the master often
is only one to two years,

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:14.740
so the cost will be lower,
there you can then get

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:17.240
also all these benefits without incurring

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:18.073
all the cost.

00:11:18.073 --> 00:11:20.720
This is in the end how I did
it, and reflecting on this

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:23.730
it did make a lot of sense
for my personal career,

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:26.070
and also looking back at some of my peers,

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:29.170
many people followed a similar
route and it worked out

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:31.750
quite well for them as far as I can tell.

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:33.700
So now I'd like to hear from you.

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:35.460
What are your experiences?

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:38.560
Did you study at a public
or a private university?

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:40.900
If you studied at a private university,

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:42.040
what are your reflections?

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:44.210
Was it really worth your money?

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:46.820
I'd love to hear from you,
and indeed as you know

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:48.880
every comment that you
leave below the video

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:50.580
also helps me with the algorithm.

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:53.490
And indeed, if you took
any value out of this video

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:55.960
at all, please hit the like button

